{
  "$comment": [
    "WHAT WAS ACTUALLY WRITTEN INTO THE FIGMA FILE.",
    "",
    "dist/figma-descriptions.json is what the build GENERATES. This file records what",
    "was APPLIED, by running figma/apply-descriptions.js against the file. The two are",
    "different claims, and until this file existed nothing checked the second one:",
    "Avatar Gradient was mapped, generated a block, and sat in Figma with an empty",
    "description while every gate in the repo passed.",
    "",
    "The hash covers the block with its version line removed. The version changes on",
    "every release, and re-applying 38 descriptions to change one number is a chore",
    "that would get skipped — and a gate people skip is not a gate. A mismatch here",
    "therefore means the SNIPPET changed: a renamed prop, a new variant, a new slot.",
    "That is exactly when Figma is showing a reader something false.",
    "",
    "To update: apply the blocks via figma/apply-descriptions.js, confirm the audit",
    "returns 0 missing, then run: pnpm --filter ionbase-ui figma:applied"
  ],
